---
// ar-va.com: who I am and what I make (2026-11-28, user: the main domain is the landing page; brand.ar-va.com stays the
// reference for the design language and how the leaf is drawn). Written as Artur, in the first person. Positioning:
// .agents/product-marketing.md. The blog's list returns here when the blog is public again (shared/site.ts).
import Layout from '@shared/layouts/Layout.astro';
import LeafMark from '@shared/components/LeafMark.astro';
import Writing from '../components/Writing.astro';
import { MAIN_SITE_PUBLIC } from '@shared/site';

const products = [
  {
    name: 'music.ar-va.com', href: 'https://music.ar-va.com', status: '', line: 'A record shelf anyone can browse',
    text: 'Collectors keep their vinyl on Discogs, a catalogue written for other collectors. I put the same collection on a shelf as covers, and every album page plays the album, so a friend who has never heard of a record can hear it first.',
  },
  {
    name: 'vincent.ar-va.com', href: 'https://vincent.ar-va.com', status: '', line: 'Nextcloud in your colours',
    text: 'Nextcloud’s own settings start from one colour. Vincent turns the colours you like into a whole light and dark theme, checks every text colour against its background, and hands you the exact settings to paste in.',
  },
  {
    name: 'anon.ar-va.com', href: 'https://anon.ar-va.com', status: '', line: 'Room to say the hard thing',
    text: 'One text box for telling me what is hard to say out loud. It never asks who you are, and a private link brings back my answer.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Solaris', href: '', status: 'In progress', line: 'A tattoo studio in one system',
    text: 'Artists, the manager and the front desk each keep their own part of a studio running. I’m building Solaris to join those parts and take on the routine work, while every decision stays with the people who run the studio.',
  },
];

const habits = [
  { title: 'Start with what’s missing', text: 'Every product I make begins with something people already want and can’t get, or get only in a form they give up on.' },
  { title: 'Build for the person who isn’t an expert', text: 'I build for the friend who doesn’t collect records, the admin who isn’t a designer, the person who is afraid to speak, the artist who would rather tattoo than do paperwork.' },
  { title: 'Put the effort underneath', text: 'I over-build the details on purpose. On music.ar-va.com the record turns at 33⅓ revolutions a minute and drops the needle with a sound made in the browser. Vincent’s tests run about a thousand generated themes through every contrast check. None of it asks for attention: it is there so the part you touch can stay simple and feel good to use.' },
  { title: 'Leave people the last word', text: 'My software does the routine work and you make the calls: your colours, whether your message goes public, how your studio runs.' },
];

const link = 'text-kikyo-600 dark:text-kikyo-400 underline underline-offset-3 hover:text-zinc-900 dark:hover:text-white';
const body = 'text-lg text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-pretty';
const h2 = 'font-bold text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-zinc-900 dark:text-white';
---
<Layout title="ARVA: what was missing, made well" description="I’m Artur. I make my own software for things people want and can’t find: a record shelf anyone can browse, Nextcloud in your colours, a safe place to say the hard thing, and Solaris for tattoo studios.">
  <main class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 w-full pt-12 pb-24">
    <header class="grid gap-8 sm:grid-cols-[minmax(0,14rem)_1fr] sm:items-center">
      <LeafMark class="w-32 sm:w-full h-auto" />
      <div>
        <h1 class="font-bold text-4xl sm:text-5xl text-zinc-900 dark:text-white text-balance">What was missing, made well</h1>
        <p class={`mt-4 max-w-2xl ${body}`}>
          I’m Artur, and ARVA is where I make my own software for things people want and can’t find, or can only find done
          badly. Each product is simple to use, carefully engineered underneath, and made to outlast the trend it was built in.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="work">
      <h2 id="work" class={h2}>The work</h2>
      <ul class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {products.map((p) => (
          <li class:list={['relative rounded-xl border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 bg-white dark:bg-night-surface p-6', p.href && 'hover:border-zinc-500 has-[a:focus-visible]:outline-2 has-[a:focus-visible]:outline-offset-2 has-[a:focus-visible]:outline-kikyo-500']}>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-1">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-xl text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">
                {p.href ? <a href={p.href} class="after:absolute after:inset-0 focus-visible:outline-none">{p.name}</a> : p.name}
              </h3>
              {p.status && <span class="rounded-md bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">{p.status}</span>}
            </div>
            <p class="mt-1 font-medium text-zinc-800 dark:text-zinc-200">{p.line}</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 text-pretty">{p.text}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="habits">
      <h2 id="habits" class={h2}>How I build</h2>
      <dl class="mt-8 grid gap-x-10 gap-y-8 sm:grid-cols-2 max-w-4xl">
        {habits.map((w) => (
          <div>
            <dt class="font-medium text-lg text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">{w.title}</dt>
            <dd class="mt-1.5 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 text-pretty">{w.text}</dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-20 max-w-3xl" aria-labelledby="leaf">
      <h2 id="leaf" class={h2}>The leaf</h2>
      <p class={`mt-4 ${body}`}>
        My sign is an oak leaf, <i>kashiwa</i> in Japanese. The kashiwa oak keeps its leaves all winter and lets them go
        only when the new ones open, and I make my products to hold on the same way, until something better is ready to
        take their place.
      </p>
      <p class={`mt-4 ${body}`}>
        <a class={link} href="https://brand.ar-va.com/story">How the leaf is drawn from 18 circles</a> and <a class={link} href="https://brand.ar-va.com/">the rules all my products follow</a> are on brand.ar-va.com.
      </p>
    </section>

    {MAIN_SITE_PUBLIC && <div class="mt-20"><Writing /></div>}
  </main>
</Layout>
